            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0449" n="384" xml:id="pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.711/31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Merriam</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-14T15:00:00-05:00">November 14, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Your 59, November 12, 9 p.m. The Department perceives no objection to an
                    informal and personal inquiry such as you suggest. However, you should avoid
                    initiating discussion of possible restrictions on “offending periodicals” or
                    suggesting other concessions which might subsequently hamper the Department in
                    making representations in behalf of American publishers, either individually or
                    collectively.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
